<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Legacy auto-backup rules. Android only consults this file on API 24-30; from API 31 the platform
   uses data_extraction_rules.xml instead. `minSdk` is 24 (app/build.gradle.kts), so a majority of
   installable devices still take this path.

   Regression being pinned (F-LEGAL-002): this element used to be empty, which means "back up
   everything". On API 24-30 that uploaded the Room database — users, devices, orders and the phone
   number recorded in UserEntity — to the user's Google Drive, with no notice in PRIVACY_FA.md and
   no equivalent on newer devices. The excludes below mirror data_extraction_rules.xml exactly.

   Local Room records are a cache, not an account backup. Server data is restored after sign-in.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="database" path="." />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
